# Database & Migrations

## Schema reference

- Source of truth: `supabase/COMPLETE_SCHEMA_DUMP.sql` (production schema dump)
- Migration workflow: `supabase/MIGRATION_STRATEGY.md`
- Do NOT reference `supabase/archive/` (outdated)

## Creating migrations

1. Create the file in `supabase/migrations/` with timestamp format `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_description.sql`
2. Apply it via Supabase MCP (`execute_sql` / `apply_migration`)
3. NEVER auto-update `supabase/COMPLETE_SCHEMA_DUMP.sql` — the user regenerates schema docs after the migration is applied

## New core tables

If client queries will depend on the table:

1. Map it in `TABLE_TO_KEYS` in `src/lib/query/keys.ts`
2. Add it to realtime: `ALTER PUBLICATION supabase_realtime ADD TABLE public.<table>;`
